      "title": "Separate four questions about the policy",
      "narration": "Marcus wants protection while his children are financially dependent. A term policy covers a specified period if the contract stays in force. Ordinary term generally has no cash accumulation. Ask four separate questions: how long protection lasts, how the death benefit changes, how long the premium is guaranteed, and what rights exist afterward. A level benefit does not by itself promise a level premium forever. Read the schedules. Maryland also requires clear language about whether a death on the term's expiry date is covered. A single word such as term cannot settle all those questions.",
