      "title": "Level benefit and level premium are different",
      "narration": "A stated twenty-year policy keeps a five hundred thousand dollar death benefit and a guaranteed annual premium of six hundred dollars during that period. The benefit and premium are both level under these particular terms. If the contract permits renewal afterward at a higher scheduled rate, that does not extend the original six hundred dollar guarantee. Annual renewable term uses one-year periods and commonly increases its renewal premium as the insured ages. A lower starting premium should be compared with future costs and the length of the need, not treated as the price for every future year.",
